    "In a Claisen–Schmidt reaction, acetone and benzaldehyde are stirred with NaOH in aqueous ethanol (Figure 1). After each aldol addition, the β-hydroxy ketone loses water to form a C=C double bond conjugated with both the C=O and the benzene ring. Because acetone has α-hydrogens on both sides, it can react twice.",
